<tbx style="dca" type="TBX-Basic" xml:lang="en" xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:30042:ed-2">
  <tbxHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <source>https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0001</source>
    </fileDesc>
  </tbxHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <conceptEntry id="dpp-0001">
      <languageSection xml:lang="eng">
          <descrip type="definition">
            <p>a concept or technology which enables sharing of product related information that is essential for product sustainability and circularity, including those specified in regulations, across all relevant economic actors</p>
          </descrip>
          <note type="note">Example characteristics include environmental sustainability, environmental impact, and recyclability.</note>
          <note type="note">Definitional conflict: the EN 182xx series (18216, 18221, 18222, 18223, 18239, 18246) define DPP as a &quot;digital record of product characteristics throughout its life cycle&quot; — differing in noun (concept/technology vs record) and in stated scope (across relevant economic actors vs throughout the life cycle).</note>
          <note type="note">Definitional variant: EN 18219:2026 (§3.1.3) and EN 18220:2026 (§3.6) extend the EN-family definition with &quot;accessible via electronic means through a data carrier&quot; — a functional statement of the carrier subset of the ISO concept.</note>
          <ref>ISO/AWI 25534-1 (2026-09-05 draft) 3.1</ref>
          <ref>EN 18223:2026 3.4</ref>
          <ref>EN 18216:2026 3.7</ref>
          <ref>EN 18221:2026 3.2</ref>
          <ref>EN 18222:2026 3.2</ref>
          <ref>EN 18239 (prEN 18239:2025) 3.9</ref>
          <ref>EN 18246 (prEN 18246:2025) 3.2</ref>
          <ref>EN 18219:2026 3.1.3</ref>
          <ref>EN 18220:2026 3.6</ref>
      </languageSection>
      </conceptEntry>
    </body>
  </text>
</tbx>
